---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Friday — AI Teammates for Product Teams — Pratyush Shrivastav"
  description="AI teammates that accelerate product discovery, scoping, prototyping, and documentation. Specialized workflows for modern product teams."
>
  <section class="work-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <div class="work-breadcrumb reveal">
        <a href="/">← Back to home</a>
      </div>

      <div class="work-head reveal">
        <span class="kicker kicker--accent">Friday</span>
        <h1 class="work-title display">
          AI teammates for modern product teams.
        </h1>
        <p class="work-lede">
          Discovery. Scoping. Prototyping. Documentation. Friday is a collection of specialized AI workflows that remove repetitive work and accelerate product execution across the entire software lifecycle.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-content">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Insight</h2>
        <p>
          Product development has a repetitive skeleton: discover the problem, scope the solution, prototype and validate, document what you built.
        </p>
        <p>
          These phases aren't where thinking happens. They're where documentation happens. The thinking is done. The decisions are made. What's left is synthesis, organization, and articulation.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is exactly what AI is good at. Not thinking. But helping humans think faster by handling the synthesis.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Most "AI for product teams" tools treat AI as a substitute for judgment. They try to make the decisions, which is where they fail.
        </p>
        <p>
          Friday works differently. It amplifies judgment instead of replacing it. It handles the work that comes <em>after</em> decisions are made.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Core Workflows</h2>
        <p>
          Friday is built as a collection of specialized workflows, each designed for a specific phase of product development:
        </p>
        <div class="principle-list">
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Discovery Synthesizer</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Interview transcripts, research notes, user feedback. Output: Organized insights, patterns, and a prioritized problem thesis.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Scope Guardian</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Feature ideas, user requests, technical constraints. Output: A prioritized scope document with clear boundaries and exclusions.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Prototype Generator</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Feature specifications and design direction. Output: Interactive prototypes in code, ready to show to users.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Spec Composer</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Design files, technical decisions, feature list. Output: Clear, actionable specifications for engineering teams.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Roadmap Architect</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Strategic goals, constraints, priorities. Output: A phased roadmap with clear outcomes and dependencies.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle-item">
            <h3>Documentation Engine</h3>
            <p>
              Input: Code, decisions, designs. Output: Comprehensive, well-organized documentation that actually stays current.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Design Principles</h2>
        <ul class="content-list">
          <li><strong>Amplify, don't replace</strong> — AI handles synthesis. Humans handle judgment. Neither replaces the other.</li>
          <li><strong>Speed up iteration</strong> — Friday's value is velocity. Get to your next decision faster.</li>
          <li><strong>Maintain context</strong> — Each workflow understands the project context and builds on previous decisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Reversible outputs</strong> — Everything Friday generates is a starting point, not a destination. Easy to modify, reject, or rewrite.</li>
          <li><strong>Integrated, not isolated</strong> — Friday lives in your existing tools (Slack, Figma, GitHub) not in a separate dashboard.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>The Vision</h2>
        <p>
          Today, product teams spend 30-40% of their time on synthesis work that doesn't require strategic judgment—writing specs, organizing notes, generating prototypes, documenting decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Friday's ambition is simple: reduce that to 10%. Give product teams back 20-30 hours per month. Let them spend that time thinking, making decisions, and talking to users.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-style: italic;">
          The goal isn't fewer product teams. It's product teams that have time to be strategic instead of operational.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .work-hero {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .work-content {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(3rem, 10vh, 5rem);
  }

  .hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vh, 2rem);
  }

  .work-breadcrumb a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 250ms;
  }
  .work-breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .work-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.2rem);
    max-width: 16ch;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .work-lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.4vh, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .content-block p em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .principle-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .principle-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .principle-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--paper-alt);
  }

  .principle-item h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .principle-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .content-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .content-list li {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .content-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .content-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
</style>
